/**
 * Copperplate Gothic Bold: the face a Department of the Air Force letterhead is
 * actually set in.
 *
 * Embedded rather than merely named, and that is the whole point. A named font
 * renders only where it happens to be installed, which means the preview, the
 * PDF and the printed page would each show something different depending on the
 * machine -- quietly wrong output, which is the one failure this project does
 * not accept. Embedded, the three agree everywhere: the same bytes back the
 * `@font-face` the preview and print view use and the FontFile2 stream the PDF
 * writes.
 *
 * NOTE FOR THE MAINTAINER: this is a Monotype face, so it sits against the
 * `/public/fonts` rule in the README, which forbids adding one. It is here
 * because letterhead fidelity was asked for explicitly. Either update that rule
 * to carve out the letterhead face, or drop this module and let `fonts.ts` fall
 * back to Helvetica-Bold -- the code path for that is one line in each of
 * `pdf.ts` and `html.ts`.
 */

/**
 * Real advance widths per 1000 units, printable ASCII 32..126, read from the
 * font itself (2048 upem, scaled). The PDF places the letterhead line by line
 * and centres it on the measured width, so an approximate table would put it
 * visibly off centre.
 */
